<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: First Maryland Q1 earnings up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>First Maryland Q1 earnings up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>		    Three mnths to Mar 97  Three mnths to Mar 96</p>
<p> Net Income		   34.10		  vs 30.07</p>
<p> Net interest income	104.40		 vs 99.87</p>
<p>Total interest/div</p>
<p> income			 184.62		 vs 182.97</p>
<p> Total interest expense   80.21		  vs 83.09</p>
<p>Income before income</p>
<p> tax			    53.30		  vs 46.18</p>
<p>NOTE - FMB said the earnings highlights included loan growth of nine percent and deposit growth of 10 percent. It said strong growth in non-interest income of 23 percent primarily related to service charges on deposit accounts and trust and investment advisory fees.</p>
<p>It said increases in expenses were held to just over three percent and included costs of First Washington and Zirkin-Cutler.</p>
<p>NOTE - First Maryland Bancorp is a wholly-owned U.S. unit of Ireland's Allied Irish Banks Plc.</p>
</text>
